---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Explorer from '../../components/embedding/Explorer';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  name: 'CPCG Embedding Explorer',
  applicationCategory: 'EducationalApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Web',
  description:
    'Embed Cartesian products of complete graphs on Chimera and Pegasus. Remove qubits and couplings and inspect verified chain mappings.',
};
---

<BaseLayout title="CPCG Embedding Explorer" description={schema.description} schema={schema}>
  <p class="mb-6"><a class="text-link" href="/research/#tools">← Explore the work</a></p>
  <p class="eyebrow">Quantum computing / Interactive laboratory</p>
  <h1 class="mt-4">CPCG embedding explorer</h1>
  <p class="intro-copy">
    A logical variable can take several physical qubits. Explore how a Cartesian product of complete
    graphs fits onto Pegasus or Chimera, then remove hardware and see how the chains change.
  </p>
  <Explorer client:load />
  <noscript><p>This explorer needs JavaScript to construct and check embeddings.</p></noscript>
  <section class="zephyr-challenge" aria-labelledby="zephyr-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The next topology</p><h2 id="zephyr-heading">
        Zephyr: an open CPCG challenge.
      </h2>
      <p>The Zephyr counterpart of this structured CPCG construction is still open here.</p>
    </div>
    <a href="mailto:anwildri@fnal.gov?subject=Zephyr%20CPCG%20embedding"
      >Unsolved! Wanna solve it? Contact me! ↗</a
    >
  </section>
  <details class="embedding-method">
    <summary>How the embeddings are constructed and checked</summary>
    <p>
      The starting mappings adapt the nexus-and-bus constructions in my
      <a href="https://github.com/AWildridge/PrimaryVertexing">PrimaryVertexing code</a>. The
      logical graph is K<sub>m</sub> □ K<sub>n</sub>: m × n variables with a clique in every row and
      column. This is the structure that appears when assigning tracks to candidate vertices.
    </p>
    <p>
      Hardware graphs use D-Wave’s standard Chimera and Pegasus connectivity and integer qubit IDs.
      Start with ideal hardware, then disable individual qubits or couplings. The explorer tries
      unused paths and alternative placements; it checks that every chain is connected, that chains
      are disjoint, and that every logical edge has a working physical coupling before allowing
      export.
    </p>
    <p>
      The browser search is bounded and does not guarantee an optimal embedding. Zephyr’s general
      embedding tools already exist; the challenge above concerns this structured CPCG construction.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://docs.dwavequantum.com/en/latest/quantum_research/topologies.html"
        >D-Wave topology reference ↗</a
      >
    </p>
  </details>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .intro-copy {
    max-width: 51rem;
    margin-top: 1.3rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-muted));
    font-size: 1.12rem;
  }
  .zephyr-challenge {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-border));
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-accent) / 0.035);
  }
  .zephyr-challenge h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .zephyr-challenge p:not(.eyebrow) {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-muted));
  }
  .zephyr-challenge a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
    max-width: 15rem;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }
  .embedding-method {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: rgb(var(--color-muted));
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .embedding-method summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: rgb(var(--color-fg));
  }
  .embedding-method p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    max-width: 55rem;
  }
  .embedding-method a {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .zephyr-challenge {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: start;
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
    .zephyr-challenge a {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }
</style>
